                        "type": "0",
                        "version": 0,
                        "content": "The nurse is assessing the respiratory status of a client who has suffered a fractured rib. The nurse would expect to note which finding?",
                        "subjectId": "ad5ab04c79144c0ea9b83385308c3b1d",
                        "difficultyIds": "11797937e327eb6d913faa80427c566b",
                        "difficulty": "考试范围-Analyzing 分析",
                        "textAnalysis": "Rationale:\nRib fractures result from a blunt injury or a fall. Typical signs and symptoms include pain and tenderness localized at the fracture site that is exacerbated by inspiration and palpation, shallow respirations, splinting or guarding the chest protectively to minimize chest movement, and possible bruising at the fracture site. Paradoxical respirations are seen with flail chest.",
                        "id": "26b13660219d45a6abcfd3e08e5e29c6",
                        "mark": "0",
                        "collectionState": "0"
                    },
                    {
                        "optionList": [
                            {
                                "isRight": "0",
                                "userAnswer": "",
                                "isSelected": "0",
                                "id": "bbba48328f4e4645abf800feb97da08c",
                                "content": "Inhalation of pathogens in the air"
                            },
                            {
                                "isRight": "0",
                                "userAnswer": "",
                                "isSelected": "0",
                                "id": "79fed438b9d5460d89d5fa31f3d64966",
                                "content": "Aspiration of microbes from the oropharynx"
                            },
                            {
                                "isRight": "0",
                                "userAnswer": "",
                                "isSelected": "0",
                                "id": "f6fe0ff7aea340e0baa2d35a08c7e5da",
                                "content": "Aspiration of microbes from the nasopharynx"
                            },
                            {
                                "isRight": "1",
                                "userAnswer": "",
                                "isSelected": "0",
                                "id": "21002ad1a552434ea25be4bdb7b509f7",
                                "content": "Develops from a primary infection at a different site in the body"
                            }
                        ],
                        "extJson": {
                            "optionList": [
                                {
